<manifest>
  <!--
    Deliberately does NOT declare com.google.mlkit.vision.DEPENDENCIES.

    That key is shared: expo-camera declares it as "barcode_ui", and
    expo-dev-launcher does the same in its debug manifest. A library adding a
    different value for the same android:name is not a merge, it is a conflict,
    and the Android manifest merger fails the build outright.

    Since only one value can win, it has to be assembled where the whole app is
    visible. See app.plugin.js in this module, which writes the combined list
    into the application manifest with tools:replace.
  -->
</manifest>
